{"user": "my first move b7 flipped 5 discs but white had a8 ready. in endgame is it better to avoid giving the opponent a corner even if you flip more discs?", "user_ts": "2026-08-12T22:10:22.223057+00:00", "assistant": "Usually **yes**: in the endgame, **don\u2019t value \u201cflips now\u201d too highly** if the move gives White a **corner**.\n\nWhy:\n\n- Discs you flip now can often be flipped back.\n- A **corner is permanent**.\n- A corner often makes the whole nearby edge stable for White.\n- So a move like **b7 next to a8** can be dangerous if it gives White **a8**.\n\nBut it\u2019s **not automatic**. In the final few moves, the real question is:  \n**\u201cAfter White takes the corner, do I still win the final count?\u201d**\n\nIn your game, Black still finished **41\u201323**, so even though White got **a8**, it didn\u2019t cost enough to matter. The key lesson: **avoid gifting corners unless you\u2019ve counted that the trade still wins.**", "assistant_started_ts": "2026-08-12T22:10:22.223057+00:00", "assistant_ts": "2026-08-12T22:10:27.223057+00:00", "annotation_user": {"final": ["Think Aloud", "Knowledge Deficit Question"], "consensus": ["Think Aloud", "Knowledge Deficit Question"], "votes": {"Think Aloud": 3, "Solution Request": 1, "Knowledge Deficit Question": 2}, "confidence": {"Think Aloud": 1.0, "Solution Request": 0.3333333333333333, "Knowledge Deficit Question": 0.6666666666666666}, "per_model": {"gpt": ["Think Aloud", "Solution Request"], "llama": ["Think Aloud", "Knowledge Deficit Question"], "sonnet": ["Think Aloud", "Knowledge Deficit Question"]}, "n_valid": 3, "min_votes": 2, "no_majority": false, "needs_review": false, "arbiter_used": false}, "annotation_assistant_fine": {"final": ["Board Report", "Local Justification", "General Principle"], "consensus": ["Board Report", "Local Justification", "General Principle"], "votes": {"Board Report": 2, "Local Justification": 3, "General Principle": 3, "Prompt": 1, "Hint": 1}, "confidence": {"Board Repo